Chapter: LiteralMatchOpen
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A match on a literal with no catch-all arm used to compile clean and answer
 its LAST arm for a value no arm names: `pick 3` below printed 20. A literal
 match on Integer, Text, Char or Real is exhaustive only through a catch-all,
 and a Boolean match only when it names both values.

Section: Body

  pick : Integer -> Integer
  pick (n) = when n is 1 -> 10 is 2 -> 20

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (pick 3))
  end

